The cancellation lemma is now stronger than expected: after the one-variable bound, a short global differential identity eliminates every remaining cancellation band, including the order-five Davenport extremals. This makes the degree bound unconditional once a depressed global cubic exists. I’m recording the monogenicity criterion first, because that is the surviving logical bottleneck.
